WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:03.880
Let's go next to our caller from the two five,
six area code.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:06.610
Who's calling today from two five, six.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.960
This is Alex.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.090
How's it going, man?

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:15.219
Hey Alex, what's up?

00:00:15.219 --> 00:00:21.250
Not most man, a big fan of your show and I
appreciate what you do, but I just wanted

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.399
to get your opinion.

00:00:22.399 --> 00:00:24.599
Uh, free education.

00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:28.359
Uh, I live in Huntsville and it's a military
town.

00:00:28.359 --> 00:00:33.172
It's got the Redstone arsenal, employs many
people, but I just thought it was on my mind.

00:00:33.172 --> 00:00:35.850
Like how do you think that would affect military
enrollment?

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.309
Uh, I know that some people do it for love
of country, but nowadays people do it more

00:00:40.309 --> 00:00:46.350
so for, I feel like for the, uh, incentives,
you know, as far as education, healthcare.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.230
So I wanted to get your opinion on that.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.140
Yeah, I have a segment about this.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:55.350
It's called something like wouldn't free college
and healthcare decimate military recruiting

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.760
or something like that.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:03.659
And it's certainly plausible, but military
recruiting would be, um, affected if, uh,

00:01:03.659 --> 00:01:07.250
the economic incentives are the reason that
a lot of people are joining.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.020
There are questions as to what percentage
of people who join the military are actually

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:12.189
joining for those reasons.

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:16.250
But here's the, the big argument for me, I
want people in the military who actually want

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:17.250
to be in the military.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.930
I don't want someone joining the military
out of desperation because they need healthcare.

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:22.330
So I actually think that

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:24.260
the reality these days,

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:25.260
right, absolutely.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:29.549
And I think even if it's true, I don't think
we are well served by having people in the

00:01:29.549 --> 00:01:33.860
military who don't actually want to be there
except that it's how they figured out they

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.310
could afford college and get healthcare.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.579
So if it's true, I don't think it's a bad
thing.

00:01:37.579 --> 00:01:40.189
The military is more than big enough.

00:01:40.189 --> 00:01:41.560
Right.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:42.560
And uh, one more thing.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.119
I have a recommendation if, uh, again, getting
ahead of myself, but if, if Bernie Sanders

00:01:47.119 --> 00:01:50.340
wins crystal ball, man, she needs to be a
press secretary.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:51.340
Okay.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:52.340
All right.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:53.840
Maybe that, uh, I'll, I'll ask her about that.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:54.840
I'm in touch with crystal.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:55.840
We'll see.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:56.840
We'll see about that.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:57.840
That would be very interesting.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:58.840
Uh, all right.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:01:59.840
Thank you so much for the call.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:00.840
Very much appreciate hearing from you.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:00.853
Let's go next to our caller from the six eight
two area code.

